From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <DCHEM88@hotmail.it>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 11:18:44 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 37/37] security/memory: Do not report clearing address zero as
 a NULL dereference

With SECURITY_CLEAR_DRAM_ON_REGULAR_BOOT and the default
DEBUG_NULL_DEREF_BREAKPOINTS, every regular boot logs

  clear_memory: Clearing DRAM 0000000000000000-0000000000005000
  Null dereference at eip: ...

The eip is the rep stos of memset(): the first RAM range starts at
address zero, and clearing it is what the code is meant to do. Remove
the breakpoints while DRAM is cleared and place them again afterwards.

TEST=On a ThinkPad W541 the error was logged at every boot, pointing at
memset() in ramstage. Built lenovo/w541 with the change.

Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018n3yuWwDLW63F4vdf7ZFTv
---
 src/security/memory/memory_clear.c | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/security/memory/memory_clear.c b/src/security/memory/memory_clear.c
index e747f4f3c..a67e2432f 100644
--- a/src/security/memory/memory_clear.c
+++ b/src/security/memory/memory_clear.c
@@ -1,6 +1,7 @@
 /* SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only */
 
 #if ENV_X86
+#include <arch/null_breakpoint.h>
 #include <cpu/x86/pae.h>
 #else
 #define memset_pae(a, b, c, d, e) 0
@@ -8,6 +9,8 @@
 #define PAE_PGTL_SIZE 0
 #define PAE_VMEM_ALIGN 0
 #define PAE_VMEM_SIZE 0
+static inline void null_breakpoint_init(void) {}
+static inline void null_breakpoint_remove(void) {}
 #endif
 
 #include <memrange.h>
@@ -100,6 +103,12 @@ static void clear_memory(void *unused)
 		__func__, (void *)pgtbl, (void *)vmem_addr);
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * The first range starts at address zero: clearing it is not a NULL
+	 * dereference, so keep the breakpoint that reports them out of the way.
+	 */
+	null_breakpoint_remove();
+
 	/* Now clear all usable DRAM */
 	memranges_each_entry(r, &mem) {
 		if (range_entry_tag(r) != BM_MEM_RAM)
@@ -135,6 +144,8 @@ static void clear_memory(void *unused)
 		memset((void *)pgtbl, 0, PAE_PGTL_SIZE);
 	}
 
+	null_breakpoint_init();
+
 	memranges_teardown(&mem);
 }
 
